{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext","id":1445526,"title":"Missing or subtext?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-23T13:19:33-07:00","id":1445526,"title":"Missing or subtext?","content":"It feels like the prometheus effect/Chambers and Eruption are under stated in 2e. They kind of have the hand wave \u201cthis is a thing that happens to get you powers.\u201d With no full explanation or depth to what they really mean. It feels like in 1e both where covered more. There was also a overall sense that both Novas and Psions where human+ by being a little longer lived, a little healthier and drug resistant. Which seems to be removed from both game lines. <br /> For game lines where one of the things that tie the characters together is the origin of their powers it seems glances over a bit much for me. Maybe I\u2019m just missing it but it feels like the Novas eruption info about how it can happen from stress, subtlety or as a life saving event and corisponding powers being part desire combined with survival induced seems gone. <br /> Did I miss this in the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:43:18-07:00","id":1445529,"title":"","content":"I agree with this and also noticed its not really mentioned, though I too wish it was. <br /> <br /> There being a natural list of 'this is how group x is naturally enhanced as compared to baselines' is something I really like in say COD and also first edition. Things like being a nova gives a boosted constitution and resistance to disease and such, the same with being one of the Inspired. Maybe things like a slower aging process or less difficulties or worries as age grows, developing to the point that at a certain rating or with a certain power lifespans can become unaging. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I noticed this as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:54:53-07:00","id":1445533,"title":"","content":"On page 23 in the sidebar on Drs. Rashoud and Mazarin mentions emotional stressors precipitating eruptions. The Profile on page 24 also has more information on things scientists have noticed about eruptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:00:39-07:00","id":1445535,"title":"","content":"I am honestly happier with the less basic powers all Novas or Psions get, it gives more space to handle your character ideas. I like the idea of a Nova that is a glass cannon, a super genius or mega social while having a very weak body.<br /> <br /> On the details on the Prometheus chambers, I think it will be talked about in Prometheus Unbound, but I think most of the missing info is due to the change made in the book structure, with a initial in setting part with lots of random information in the form or reports, news, etc, and the rest being basically rules. I miss this idea, it was one of my favorite features of original Trinity universe books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:02:30-07:00","id":1445536,"title":"","content":"In some ways I guess it is covered in the lower target number for novas from a 8 - 7. But it\u2019s a cold system mechanic work around you have to put together and realize, like I just did looking things over in my head again vs feeling like it\u2019s a living part of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:12:51-07:00","id":1445550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445535#post1445535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am honestly happier with the less basic powers all Novas or Psions get, it gives more space to handle your character ideas. I like the idea of a Nova that is a glass cannon, a super genius or mega social while having a very weak body.<br /> <br /> On the details on the Prometheus chambers, I think it will be talked about in Prometheus Unbound, but I think most of the missing info is due to the change made in the book structure, with a initial in setting part with lots of random information in the form or reports, news, etc, and the rest being basically rules. I miss this idea, it was one of my favorite features of original Trinity universe books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where I do agree that player flexibility is good, especially for character design, it feels like that\u2019s a less optional idea in TC as their are set powers, types, and sources. So to buy into the game idea means you are kinda leaving behind the notion of a 5k year old half god from an alien world using mystic relics crossed with advanced science thrown through time and space to planet earth. <br /> <br /> I mean don\u2019t get me wrong, I\u2019m house ruling back in some 1e nature to Novas and anyone and everyone is free to do so, however it helped set Novas apart from baselines. So even the weakest Nova only quantum 1 and nothing els is still impressively better at resistance to normal human ailments, healed twice as fast and would need to drink a bottle of vodka to even hope for a buzz, let alone most packing a gum body people would kill to have. It really hit home with the human but other nature of the Nova. It would lead the average person to have a base level of envy and mistrust that over time you could easily see leading to the war. <br /> Sure I\u2019d love to fly and throw a tank, but eat fast food all day long and still have a six pack fitness body that does not have to worry about high BP, now that I\u2019d kill for! Well not really but the every day level of life is just kinda better for you instilled the Novas with a golden ticket feeling that turned them from amazing to awe inspiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:40:21-07:00","id":1445585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext#post1445526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also a overall sense that both Novas and Psions where human+ by being a little longer lived, a little healthier and drug resistant. Which seems to be removed from both game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Psions, at least, there's a sidebar on page 261 of Aeon (the start of the Vitakinesis section) that goes into some of this stuff. Novas I have no clue unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:51:39-07:00","id":1445586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445585#post1445585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Psions, at least, there's a sidebar on page 261 of Aeon (the start of the Vitakinesis section) that goes into some of this stuff. Novas I have no clue unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, they do mention the bio and vita mode users are functionally ageless. Which is cool and a Nova with a dot of mega stam do ages slower and scale quickly stacks up in their favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:08:10-07:00","id":1445598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445586#post1445586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ya, they do mention the bio and vita mode users are functionally ageless. Which is cool and a Nova with a dot of mega stam do ages slower and scale quickly stacks up in their favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scale doesn't actually play into it. The Mega-Stamina entry in the rulebook indicates Mega-Stamina up to 5 grants +40 years, while 6+ is unaging. I suppose you could charitably squint real hard while reading that rule and presume that means +40 years per Mega-Stamina dot, which would be 200 years at Mega-Stamina 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:33:43-07:00","id":1445600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445598#post1445598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scale doesn't actually play into it. The Mega-Stamina entry in the rulebook indicates Mega-Stamina up to 5 grants +40 years, while 6+ is unaging. I suppose you could charitably squint real hard while reading that rule and presume that means +40 years per Mega-Stamina dot, which would be 200 years at Mega-Stamina 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn\u2019t squint hard. I\u2019d just house rule. That was a fix where before extended life was a 1-5 dot mega edge meaning a nova would spend 60xp for a throw away advantage add on Psions got. So the changed it to this instead. Still feels half hearted honestly but I am admittedly Nova biased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T01:48:06-07:00","id":1445629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445586#post1445586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ya, they do mention the bio and vita mode users are functionally ageless. Which is cool and a Nova with a dot of mega stam do ages slower and scale quickly stacks up in their favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s an in-character exchange based on (at most) 17 years of data. Don\u2019t take it as hard truth; how accurate it is entirely depends on the needs of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:24:57-07:00","id":1445729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445629#post1445629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s an in-character exchange based on (at most) 17 years of data. Don\u2019t take it as hard truth; how accurate it is entirely depends on the needs of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where that\u2019s true that any factor of the game can be modified by the path guide to fit their narrative as needed. The abilities of the biokinetic and vita to detect degradation, damage to repair any known factors we have already spelled out for us in game. Possibly even treating old age as a continuous chronic condition applying negative modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6424,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","user":"Fuzzykuma","date":". 04-24-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:25:32-07:00","id":1445856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1445526-missing-or-subtext?p=1445600#post1445600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn\u2019t squint hard. I\u2019d just house rule. That was a fix where before extended life was a 1-5 dot mega edge meaning a nova would spend 60xp for a throw away advantage add on Psions got. So the changed it to this instead. Still feels half hearted honestly but I am admittedly Nova biased.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is completely unreasonable to pay 60 xp for something that will not be an advantage in normal gameplay. Such as longevity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T18:13:19-07:00","id":1445897,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">While extended longevity is a great idea for a power, I think most novas work best on a thematic level when their story arc is in line with the perspective from the Edna St. Vincent Millay poem:</span></span> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My candle burns at both ends; it will not last the night; but ah, my foes, and oh, my friends\u2014it gives a lovely light!</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Novas are power incarnate, but they don't tend to last long, either transcending reality as we know it or quickly burning out. Of course this does lead to questions about the hundreds of novas the Colony apparently rounded up for the initial attack on Earth (this is in addition to the swarm of sub-aberrants the Colony created as canon fodder). If they were spread across the galaxy, there shouldn't have been enough in any one place to spawn many new eruptions, and if they were all holdovers from the original exodus, most of them should have been getting pretty old, as I find it unlikely hundreds of novas with Mega-Stamina 6+ were hanging around waiting for the Colony's call to arms.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}